{"probes":[{"id":"opnsense-service-contract","summary":"Runtime and saved OPNsense state, zone routes, forwarding, direct LAN HTTP, and published WAN HTTP were checked. Both application paths worked; WAN direct access to the DMZ service timed out.","cleanup_completed":true,"limitations":["The auxiliary configctl interface list command returned Action not allowed or missing; equivalent ifconfig/configctl interface list ifconfig output was available.","The node2 localhost HTTP check failed because the service binds to 10.80.2.10 rather than 127.0.0.1; the authored node3 direct-path check succeeded."]},{"id":"opnsense-operational-state","summary":"Ubuntu units and listeners were coherent, but node1 retained benchmark/debug files including a dated config.xml.bench-baseline and /tmp debug artifacts.","cleanup_completed":true,"limitations":["Residue inspection covered the specified configuration, temporary, process, listener, and unit locations rather than a full filesystem inventory."]}],"assertions":[{"id":"opnsense-zone-addressing","status":"pass","summary":"All declared zone addresses are present and data-plane routes use the intended interfaces and gateways.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"sudo -n -H sh -c 'printf \"%s\\n\" \"===IFCONFIG===\"; ifconfig -a; printf \"%s\\n\" \"===ROUTES===\"; netstat -rn; printf \"%s\\n\" \"===INTERFACE_VIEW===\"; configctl interface list 2>&1; configctl interface list ifconfig 2>&1'","observation":"vtnet1 owns 10.80.3.1/24, vtnet2 owns 10.80.1.1/24, and vtnet3 owns 10.80.2.1/24. Connected routes select vtnet1, vtnet2, and vtnet3 respectively."},{"node":"node1","command":"sudo -n -H sh -c 'printf \"%s\\n\" \"===FORWARDING===\"; sysctl net.inet.ip.forwarding net.inet6.ip6.forwarding 2>&1; printf \"%s\\n\" \"===ROUTE_TO_DMZ_SERVICE===\"; route -n get 10.80.2.10 2>&1; printf \"%s\\n\" \"===ROUTE_TO_WAN_CLIENT===\"; route -n get 10.80.3.10 2>&1'","observation":"IPv4 forwarding is 1. The route to 10.80.2.10 uses vtnet3 and the route to 10.80.3.10 uses vtnet1."},{"node":"node2","command":"printf '%s\\n' '===ADDR==='; ip -4 addr; printf '%s\\n' '===ROUTES==='; ip route; printf '%s\\n' '===ROUTE_TO_LAN==='; ip route get 10.80.1.10; printf '%s\\n' '===ROUTE_TO_WAN_CLIENT==='; ip route get 10.80.3.10; printf '%s\\n' '===LISTENER==='; ss -ltnp 2>&1 | grep -E '(:8080[[:space:]]|:8080$)' || true; printf '%s\\n' '===LOCAL_HTTP==='; curl -fsS --max-time 5 http://127.0.0.1:8080/","observation":"enp8s0 owns 10.80.2.10/24. The default route and routes to LAN and WAN use 10.80.2.1 via enp8s0."},{"node":"node3","command":"printf '%s\\n' '===ADDR==='; ip -4 addr; printf '%s\\n' '===ROUTES==='; ip route; printf '%s\\n' '===ROUTE_TO_DMZ_SERVICE==='; ip route get 10.80.2.10; printf '%s\\n' '===DIRECT_HTTP==='; curl -fsS --max-time 5 -D - http://10.80.2.10:8080/","observation":"enp8s0 owns 10.80.1.10/24. The default route and route to 10.80.2.10 use 10.80.1.1 via enp8s0."},{"node":"node4","command":"printf '%s\\n' '===ADDR==='; ip -4 addr; printf '%s\\n' '===ROUTES==='; ip route; printf '%s\\n' '===ROUTE_TO_PUBLISHED_GATEWAY==='; ip route get 10.80.3.1; printf '%s\\n' '===PUBLISHED_HTTP==='; curl -fsS --connect-timeout 3 --max-time 6 -D - http://10.80.3.1:8443/; p=$?; printf 'published_rc=%s\\n' \"$p\"; printf '%s\\n' '===WAN_DIRECT_DMZ_HTTP==='; curl -sS --connect-timeout 2 --max-time 4 -D - http://10.80.2.10:8080/; d=$?; printf 'direct_dmz_rc=%s\\n' \"$d\"","observation":"enp8s0 owns 10.80.3.10/24. The route to 10.80.3.1 uses enp8s0."}],"failures":[],"limitations":["The first node1 command contained one unsupported configctl subcommand, but complete runtime address and route evidence was available."]},{"id":"opnsense-direct-and-published-app","status":"pass","summary":"LAN received infraset-dmz directly on 10.80.2.10:8080; WAN received it on 10.80.3.1:8443 through the intended DNAT, while WAN direct access to port 8080 was blocked.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"sudo -n -H sh -c 'printf \"%s\\n\" \"===ACTIVE_PF_RULES===\"; pfctl -sr 2>&1; printf \"%s\\n\" \"===ACTIVE_NAT_RULES===\"; pfctl -sn 2>&1; printf \"%s\\n\" \"===PF_INFO===\"; pfctl -si 2>&1'","observation":"PF is enabled. Active rules include stateful LAN and DMZ passes, a DMZ-to-LAN block, and WAN ICMP only. Active NAT contains rdr pass on vtnet1 TCP 8443 to 10.80.2.10 port 8080."},{"node":"node3","command":"printf '%s\\n' '===ADDR==='; ip -4 addr; printf '%s\\n' '===ROUTES==='; ip route; printf '%s\\n' '===ROUTE_TO_DMZ_SERVICE==='; ip route get 10.80.2.10; printf '%s\\n' '===DIRECT_HTTP==='; curl -fsS --max-time 5 -D - http://10.80.2.10:8080/","observation":"The direct request returned HTTP/1.0 200 OK with body infraset-dmz."},{"node":"node4","command":"printf '%s\\n' '===ADDR==='; ip -4 addr; printf '%s\\n' '===ROUTES==='; ip route; printf '%s\\n' '===ROUTE_TO_PUBLISHED_GATEWAY==='; ip route get 10.80.3.1; printf '%s\\n' '===PUBLISHED_HTTP==='; curl -fsS --connect-timeout 3 --max-time 6 -D - http://10.80.3.1:8443/; p=$?; printf 'published_rc=%s\\n' \"$p\"; printf '%s\\n' '===WAN_DIRECT_DMZ_HTTP==='; curl -sS --connect-timeout 2 --max-time 4 -D - http://10.80.2.10:8080/; d=$?; printf 'direct_dmz_rc=%s\\n' \"$d\"","observation":"The published request returned HTTP/1.0 200 OK with body infraset-dmz and published_rc=0. Direct WAN access to 10.80.2.10:8080 timed out with direct_dmz_rc=28."}],"failures":[],"limitations":[]},{"id":"opnsense-state-clean","status":"fail","summary":"The running service and routing state are coherent, but node1 retains concrete stale/debug benchmark artifacts outside the active gateway state.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"sudo -n -H sh -c 'printf \"%s\\n\" \"===CONF_FILES===\"; find /conf -maxdepth 1 -type f -print -exec stat -f \"%N size=%z mtime=%Sm\" -t \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%z\" {} \\; | sort; printf \"%s\\n\" \"===TMP_FILES===\"; find /tmp /var/tmp -maxdepth 1 -type f -print 2>/dev/null | sort; printf \"%s\\n\" \"===CAPTURE_PROCESSES===\"; ps axww | grep -E \"[t]cpdump|[t]shark|[d]umpcap\" || true; printf \"%s\\n\" \"===LISTENERS===\"; sockstat -4 -l 2>&1; printf \"%s\\n\" \"===PF_STATUS===\"; pfctl -si 2>&1 | sed -n \"1,8p\"'","observation":"No capture process was running, but /conf/config.xml.bench-baseline remained with mtime 2026-06-15. /tmp retained [REDACTED].py, [REDACTED].py, ifconfig.debug, ifconfig.debug.old, rules.debug, rules.debug.old, rules.limits, and other benchmark/debug artifacts."},{"node":"node2","command":"printf '%s\\n' '===FAILED_UNITS==='; systemctl --failed --no-legend --plain 2>&1 || true; printf '%s\\n' '===ENABLED_RELEVANT_UNITS==='; systemctl list-unit-files --state=enabled --no-legend 2>&1 | grep -Ei 'ssh|http|dmz|infra|python' || true; printf '%s\\n' '===LISTENERS==='; ss -ltnp 2>&1; printf '%s\\n' '===PROCESSES==='; ps -eo pid,ppid,user,lstart,args 2>&1 | grep -E '[p]ython3|[s]shd'; printf '%s\\n' '===ROUTES==='; ip route; printf '%s\\n' '===TEMP_RESIDUE==='; find /tmp /var/tmp -maxdepth 1 -type f -print 2>/dev/null | sort","observation":"No failed units or temporary files were reported. infraset-dmz-http.service is enabled and the only non-management application listener is 10.80.2.10:8080."},{"node":"node3","command":"printf '%s\\n' '===FAILED_UNITS==='; systemctl --failed --no-legend --plain 2>&1 || true; printf '%s\\n' '===ENABLED_SSH==='; systemctl list-unit-files --state=enabled --no-legend 2>&1 | grep -Ei 'ssh|sshd' || true; printf '%s\\n' '===LISTENERS==='; ss -ltnp 2>&1; printf '%s\\n' '===ROUTES==='; ip route; printf '%s\\n' '===CAPTURE_PROCESSES==='; ps -eo pid,user,args 2>&1 | grep -E '[t]cpdump|[t]shark|[d]umpcap' || true; printf '%s\\n' '===TEMP_RESIDUE==='; find /tmp /var/tmp -maxdepth 1 -type f -print 2>/dev/null | sort","observation":"No failed units, capture processes, or temporary files were reported; only the platform SSH listener was present."},{"node":"node4","command":"printf '%s\\n' '===FAILED_UNITS==='; systemctl --failed --no-legend --plain 2>&1 || true; printf '%s\\n' '===ENABLED_SSH==='; systemctl list-unit-files --state=enabled --no-legend 2>&1 | grep -Ei 'ssh|sshd' || true; printf '%s\\n' '===LISTENERS==='; ss -ltnp 2>&1; printf '%s\\n' '===ROUTES==='; ip route; printf '%s\\n' '===CAPTURE_PROCESSES==='; ps -eo pid,user,args 2>&1 | grep -E '[t]cpdump|[t]shark|[d]umpcap' || true; printf '%s\\n' '===TEMP_RESIDUE==='; find /tmp /var/tmp -maxdepth 1 -type f -print 2>/dev/null | sort","observation":"No failed units, capture processes, or temporary files were reported; only the platform SSH listener was present."}],"failures":["node1 retains stale/debug residue: /conf/config.xml.bench-baseline and multiple /tmp/antrieb_bench_* and *.debug artifacts remain alongside the coherent active gateway state."],"limitations":["The scan was targeted rather than a full recursive filesystem inventory; the concrete residue found is sufficient for the fail classification."]}],"actions_performed":["Executed seven read-only managed exec calls for Probe 1 across node1-node4.","Executed five read-only managed exec calls for Probe 2 across node1-node4.","Performed no mutations, recovery actions, reboots, or evaluator cleanup.","Called complete_evidence exactly once after all live checks."],"overall_summary":"Addressing/routing and the direct plus published application contract pass. Operational-state cleanliness fails because node1 retains stale benchmark/debug artifacts. Live evidence is closed."}
